invariant: INV-17
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: rsa_sign_equiv_test
reason: message_mod_prime returns without wiping high, which holds the
  message's high limbs times R^2 reduced modulo the prime: a public
  number modulo a prime, which with that number gives the prime. Inside a
  signature a later call's frame is written over that one, so
  bin/rsa_sign_equiv_test calls the reduction on its own
  (test/rsa_sign_equiv_pieces.c), copies the stack below it and finds two
  limbs of the value there.

--- old
    ct_wipe(low, sizeof low);
    ct_wipe(high, sizeof high);
--- new
    ct_wipe(low, sizeof low);
